      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2017 Elsevier B.V. and International Society of Chemotherapy. All rights reserved.",
        "AbstractText": "Infections due to multidrug-resistant bacteria (MDRB) are currently a clinical challenge, mainly in elderly patients. Ceftolozane/tazobactam spectrum, safety and efficacy make it an attractive option for MDRB beyond the indications approved to date. We report our experience with ceftolozane/tazobactam in 4 cases of osteomyelitis and 3 skin-soft-tissue infections due to extensively-drug-resistant Pseudomonas aeruginosa."
      },
